WEBVTT

00:00.611 --> 00:03.862
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.988 --> 00:07.257
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.291 --> 00:10.827
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.861 --> 00:13.830
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:13.864 --> 00:17.333
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.368 --> 00:20.637
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.671 --> 00:22.205
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.239 --> 00:23.573
♪ Laugh and cry

00:23.607 --> 00:27.542
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.554 --> 00:38.221
Okay, Brian, here we are.

00:38.255 --> 00:39.789
Hey, thanks for fitting in
the ride to school

00:39.824 --> 00:41.624
in between your texts.

00:41.659 --> 00:42.725
Totally, Chris, totally.

00:42.760 --> 00:44.594
I'm sure it'll all
work itself out.

00:44.628 --> 00:45.895
And good luck on that thing.

00:45.930 --> 00:48.531
You know, that was a stroller,
not a speed bump.

00:53.504 --> 00:55.138
Uh-oh. This looks like trouble.

00:55.172 --> 00:57.974
I'll know they're bullies
if they use my full name.

00:58.008 --> 00:59.309
Well, look who it is.

00:59.343 --> 01:00.510
Chris Griffin.

01:00.544 --> 01:01.511
Oh, boy.

01:01.545 --> 01:02.679
Hey, fat ass.

01:02.713 --> 01:04.447
Your boobs are bigger
than your sister's.

01:04.482 --> 01:06.249
Oh, yeah? Well...

01:06.283 --> 01:08.952
you have a sister as well.

01:08.986 --> 01:10.720
That's your comeback?

01:11.755 --> 01:12.722
Oh, man!

01:12.756 --> 01:14.824
Oh, my God. Poor Chris.

01:14.859 --> 01:17.760
He's a social outcast
like Scarface.

01:17.795 --> 01:18.995
Okay, we have a deal.

01:19.029 --> 01:21.297
You bring the money,
I get you the coke.

01:21.332 --> 01:22.966
You got it, Scarface.

01:23.000 --> 01:24.033
Oh, my God!

01:24.068 --> 01:25.368
You can see that?

01:25.402 --> 01:27.437
The doctor said
you wouldn't be able to!

01:27.471 --> 01:28.972
Yes, everyone can see that.

01:29.006 --> 01:30.406
That's why we call
you Scarface.

01:30.441 --> 01:33.343
Whoa, whoa, whoa! "We"?

01:37.848 --> 01:41.351
Well, I have officially seen
every video ever on YouTube.

01:41.385 --> 01:43.520
Got to say,
there's not a bad one.

01:43.554 --> 01:46.289
I need these shipping invoices
filed immediately.

01:46.323 --> 01:49.259
I'll be right back.

01:49.293 --> 01:50.293
There she goes again.

01:50.327 --> 01:51.394
How come she always skips out

01:51.428 --> 01:52.462
when there's work to do?

01:52.496 --> 01:54.430
She's just taking
a smoke break.

01:54.465 --> 01:56.266
A deaf person smoking.

01:56.300 --> 01:57.967
That's-that's weird.

01:58.002 --> 01:59.302
Why is that weird?

01:59.336 --> 02:00.737
That... I mean, there's
no reason that that's weird,

02:00.771 --> 02:02.672
but it-it-it is weird, right?

02:02.706 --> 02:04.374
Yes, Griffin, it's weird.

02:04.408 --> 02:06.509
Wait, so you mean to tell me,
if I ever want to get out

02:06.544 --> 02:08.344
of something, all I got
to do is take a smoke break?

02:08.379 --> 02:09.379
Well, I suppose.

02:09.413 --> 02:11.047
But you don't smoke.

02:11.081 --> 02:14.784
Well, actually I do.

02:50.254 --> 02:51.788
All right, Griffin.

02:51.822 --> 02:53.089
You're clearly a smoker.

02:53.123 --> 02:54.891
Enjoy your break.

02:54.925 --> 02:57.327
Wow, I can use smoking
to get out of anything.

02:57.361 --> 03:00.630
Finally, I'm above the law
like my 14th century ancestor

03:00.664 --> 03:03.533
King of Denmark Griffin.

03:03.567 --> 03:05.234
More wine! More women!

03:05.269 --> 03:06.636
More table!

03:13.310 --> 03:14.911
I'm having a heart attack!

03:14.945 --> 03:16.846
Is anyone at the table a doctor?

03:16.880 --> 03:17.847
I am!

03:17.881 --> 03:20.249
Come here! Hurry! Run!

03:20.284 --> 03:23.786
"But the very far-away doctor
couldn't make it in time."

03:23.821 --> 03:27.757
And that's why here in Denmark
we have very small tables.

03:34.331 --> 03:37.266
Okay, Stewie, time to
change your diaper.

03:37.301 --> 03:40.536
Ooh! Oh, smoke break!

03:40.571 --> 03:42.538
Well, this is
how Scott Caan was raised,

03:42.573 --> 03:44.574
and he turned out okay.

03:48.012 --> 03:50.213
Hey, Dad, want to hear a story
about my day at school?

03:50.247 --> 03:52.081
It's about my hot
friend Melissa.

03:52.116 --> 03:53.182
Okay.

03:53.217 --> 03:54.884
She didn't wear a
bra to school today.

03:54.918 --> 03:56.219
Okay.

03:56.253 --> 03:58.921
And someone spilled water
all over her white shirt.

03:58.956 --> 04:00.256
Okay.

04:00.290 --> 04:02.225
And it was cold, so you
could see everything.

04:02.259 --> 04:03.960
Okay.

04:03.994 --> 04:06.229
Then she left and I realized
I was all alone...

04:06.263 --> 04:08.898
Smoke break!

04:13.137 --> 04:14.370
Hey, Chris?

04:14.405 --> 04:17.173
I-I wanted to talk about
what happened at school...

04:17.207 --> 04:18.941
Is that a dead gerbil in there?

04:18.976 --> 04:20.176
That's a fur fish.

04:20.210 --> 04:21.711
It's a weird species.

04:21.745 --> 04:23.379
You put them in there,
and they swim like hell

04:23.414 --> 04:25.815
for, like, 30 seconds,
and then they go to sleep.

04:25.849 --> 04:27.684
This joker still
hasn't woken up.

04:27.718 --> 04:29.619
Get up, lazy!

04:29.653 --> 04:30.653
You know, the way those kids

04:30.688 --> 04:32.288
were picking on you
today in school.

04:32.322 --> 04:33.790
You really got to stand
up for yourself.

04:33.824 --> 04:35.825
Stewie, it's not so easy.

04:35.859 --> 04:38.428
What would you say if I said,
"Hey there, shorty"?

04:38.462 --> 04:41.297
I'd say, "Have another
doughnut, you albino gorilla."

04:41.331 --> 04:43.332
Oh, yeah? Well...

04:43.367 --> 04:45.635
you have a sister as well.

04:45.669 --> 04:49.639
Oh, Stewie, I-I could never
come up with stuff like you do.

04:49.673 --> 04:51.207
Of course not.
You're sweet and simple.

04:51.241 --> 04:53.276
But even you could learn
enough to outsmart

04:53.310 --> 04:54.777
those cretins at your school.

04:54.812 --> 04:56.312
And they'll respect you for it.

04:56.346 --> 04:58.214
In fact, I'll teach you how.

04:58.248 --> 04:59.582
Why would you do that for me?

04:59.616 --> 05:01.117
I'm your brother, Chris.

05:01.151 --> 05:02.952
We're a team and we've got
to look out for each other.

05:02.986 --> 05:05.488
Like Owl and Costello.

05:05.522 --> 05:06.756
I mean the fellow's
name on first base.

05:06.790 --> 05:08.458
Who.
The fellow playing first base.

05:08.492 --> 05:10.093
Who.
The guy on first base.

05:10.127 --> 05:12.295
Who.
I'm asking you who's on first!

05:12.329 --> 05:14.697
Who.
That's what I'm asking you!

05:14.732 --> 05:18.634
Nothing will ever be funnier
than misunderstandings.

05:24.608 --> 05:25.742
All right, Chris,
here they come.

05:25.776 --> 05:26.976
Now, remember what we practiced.

05:27.010 --> 05:28.611
Now, what are you gonna call
the one in the middle?

05:28.645 --> 05:30.313
Isosceles triangle?

05:30.347 --> 05:31.414
What?! Come on, Chris!

05:31.448 --> 05:32.482
We worked on this all night.

05:32.516 --> 05:35.284
I know! I also had
a geometry test!

05:35.319 --> 05:36.652
Well, how'd that go?

05:41.458 --> 05:42.859
Hey, look who it is.

05:42.893 --> 05:44.193
Dorky Pig.

05:44.228 --> 05:45.595
Go on, Chris. It's now or never.

05:45.629 --> 05:46.929
Let them have it.

05:46.964 --> 05:47.964
Nice muscles.

05:47.998 --> 05:50.233
What, do you belong to a gym?

05:50.267 --> 05:51.701
Oh, for God's sake, Chris.

05:51.735 --> 05:53.770
Here, put me on your back
and repeat what I say.

05:53.804 --> 05:57.440
Quick! Here they come!

05:57.474 --> 05:59.776
You're even uglier
up close, Griffin.

05:59.810 --> 06:02.278
Okay, now say...

06:02.312 --> 06:04.914
I heard you were born
out of your mom's butt.

06:04.948 --> 06:07.917
I heard that from your mom
while I was doing her.

06:07.951 --> 06:09.252
You're a butt baby.

06:09.286 --> 06:11.521
That's why you've got moles
all over your chest.

06:11.555 --> 06:13.689
Leftover birth dook.

06:15.359 --> 06:17.260
Oh, man!
Griffin schooled him!

06:17.294 --> 06:18.561
I can't believe I'm
moving tomorrow,

06:18.595 --> 06:20.863
and I won't get to see
how this works out.

06:20.898 --> 06:23.266
Wow, Stewie, we're gonna
work perfectly together.

06:23.300 --> 06:25.802
Like Sherlock
Holmes and Watson.

06:25.836 --> 06:26.969
Watson, a clue!

06:27.004 --> 06:29.038
The intruder has
tracked in a red clay,

06:29.072 --> 06:32.341
which can only be found near
London's homosexual bathhouse.

06:32.376 --> 06:33.643
Amazing, Holmes.

06:33.677 --> 06:34.744
How did you know that?

06:34.778 --> 06:37.246
Just from, like,
books and stuff.

06:40.818 --> 06:43.052
Your turn.

06:45.155 --> 06:46.889
You know, Peter, it's so nice

06:46.924 --> 06:48.624
that after all these years
we've been together,

06:48.659 --> 06:50.092
we can still...
Smoke break!

06:50.127 --> 06:52.128
What? Peter, what are you
doing down there?

06:52.162 --> 06:53.196
Nothing.

06:53.230 --> 06:54.964
Well, it doesn't
seem like nothing.

06:57.634 --> 06:59.836
Peter, since when
are you a smoker?

06:59.870 --> 07:01.270
Put that out right now!

07:01.305 --> 07:03.105
Smoking is highly addictive.

07:03.140 --> 07:04.307
I'm not addicted.

07:04.341 --> 07:05.908
I just need a couple
every hour or so,

07:05.943 --> 07:07.443
so I don't go
completely insane.

07:07.477 --> 07:09.545
Peter, that's exactly
what addicted means.

07:09.580 --> 07:11.380
You have a serious problem.

07:11.415 --> 07:12.882
Cigarettes will kill you.

07:12.916 --> 07:14.884
Relax, Lois.
I can quit any time I want.

07:14.918 --> 07:17.320
Look, I'll toss
this one out right now.

07:18.555 --> 07:21.290
I'm so sorry I threw you
out the window!

07:24.027 --> 07:26.295
Hey, man, can you keep it down?

07:26.330 --> 07:28.464
Sorry.
Wait, whose bedroom are you in?

07:28.498 --> 07:29.465
Meg's.

07:29.499 --> 07:30.633
Okay, that's fine then.

07:34.975 --> 07:36.343
Where's Dad?

07:36.377 --> 07:39.612
Your father got up early
and went for a run.

07:40.915 --> 07:42.649
Ah, nothing
like an after-run mint

07:42.683 --> 07:45.552
to get rid
of that jogger's breath.

07:45.586 --> 07:47.420
Okay, now sit down
and have some breakfast.

07:47.455 --> 07:49.255
I made your favorite--
waffles and...

07:49.290 --> 07:51.591
Hey, uh, did anybody get
the paper today?

07:55.363 --> 07:56.830
Ah, nothing
like an after-paper mint

07:56.864 --> 07:59.632
to get rid
of that paper-getting breath.

07:59.667 --> 08:01.427
You know, I feel like
these waffles could use

08:01.435 --> 08:03.303
a little fresh air.
Come on, boys.

08:03.337 --> 08:04.304
Peter, sit down.

08:04.338 --> 08:06.339
You need your breakfast.

08:15.216 --> 08:17.584
Oh, Peter,
I meant to tell you.

08:17.618 --> 08:20.220
Remember my cousin Sylvia's
husband Robert? Well...

08:20.254 --> 08:21.855
Does this story
have an end?!

08:21.889 --> 08:23.456
Peter, I just started.

08:23.491 --> 08:24.991
Oh, Meg's out of milk.
I'll get you a carton.

08:25.025 --> 08:26.059
Hey, good story, Lois.

08:26.093 --> 08:27.994
You wrapped it up nicely.

08:33.033 --> 08:34.667
I know it's technically
not illegal,

08:34.702 --> 08:37.303
but it seemed wrong when
your music teacher wrapped

08:37.338 --> 08:39.939
a trash bag around his waist
so he could change pants.

08:39.974 --> 08:42.075
Hey, Jew-bacca!

08:42.109 --> 08:45.678
Passover's stupid and I'm gonna
prove it by breaking your nose.

08:45.713 --> 08:46.913
Hey!

08:46.947 --> 08:49.015
Why don't you pick on someone
your own religion

08:49.049 --> 08:50.884
who can fight for themselves?

08:50.918 --> 08:52.285
And you're not so tough.

08:52.319 --> 08:54.387
You frequently opt
out of swim class

08:54.422 --> 08:57.123
because of your gross
microcephalic penis.

08:57.158 --> 08:58.458
It's not gross!

08:58.492 --> 08:59.659
It's special.

08:59.693 --> 09:02.429
I can use it
to reset my cable box.

09:02.463 --> 09:06.032
Hey, Chris, what you did there
for that sweaty Jew?

09:06.066 --> 09:07.634
That was really nice.

09:07.668 --> 09:09.068
Back away, foul wench!

09:09.103 --> 09:12.605
Your wide hips hold
no temptation for me!

09:12.640 --> 09:14.274
Uh... I mean...

09:14.308 --> 09:15.508
you have...

09:17.144 --> 09:18.411
...a-a vulva...

09:18.446 --> 09:20.413
and fallopian tubes.

09:20.448 --> 09:22.115
Finally!
A guy who listens!

09:22.149 --> 09:25.351
Here's my number.
Call me.

09:30.291 --> 09:32.125
Peter, when'd you
start smoking?

09:32.159 --> 09:35.028
Well, you know, at first
it was a way to get out of work,

09:35.062 --> 09:37.030
but then I discovered
it's a delightful habit

09:37.064 --> 09:39.098
that has lots of benefits.
Yeah? Like what?

09:39.133 --> 09:41.267
Like I get to punctuate
tough conversations

09:41.302 --> 09:42.902
by ashing a cigarette.

09:42.937 --> 09:44.370
Joe, your
marriage is over.

09:44.405 --> 09:47.006
Oh, please. Bonnie and I
are stronger than ever.

09:47.041 --> 09:49.275
Your marriage...

09:49.310 --> 09:51.578
is over.

09:53.080 --> 09:56.816
Well, now that you
say it with the cigarette...

10:02.857 --> 10:05.992
God, there's, like, no one hot
at this school this year.

10:06.026 --> 10:08.228
Okay, students, take your seats.

10:09.763 --> 10:11.564
First off, we have a new rule:

10:11.599 --> 10:14.634
no more asking the gym teachers
if they went to college.

10:14.668 --> 10:16.102
They did not.

10:16.136 --> 10:19.072
Next, it's time for nominations
for student body president.

10:19.106 --> 10:21.841
As of now, we have
the perpetually upbeat black kid

10:21.876 --> 10:23.409
running unopposed.

10:23.444 --> 10:26.946
Come on, yo, this is gonna be
a great year for all of us!

10:26.981 --> 10:28.181
Surely there's another student

10:28.215 --> 10:30.517
who'd like to throw
his hat in the ring.

10:30.551 --> 10:32.185
I nominate Chris Griffin!

10:34.788 --> 10:36.422
Chris, they love you.

10:36.457 --> 10:38.858
I'm a better coach
than God.

10:38.893 --> 10:41.027
Come on, you're getting
crucified out there!

10:41.061 --> 10:42.896
I know. It's
a crucifixion.

10:42.930 --> 10:44.230
Well, yeah, I know.

10:44.265 --> 10:45.832
But that doesn't mean
you should stop trying.

10:45.866 --> 10:47.901
Dad, you're not
the coach!

10:53.240 --> 10:56.543
Peter, your fart didn't
go off until 8:30.

10:56.577 --> 10:58.578
Get up. We're late!

11:01.048 --> 11:02.916
What the hell?!

11:02.950 --> 11:04.450
What? What? What?!
Peter,

11:04.485 --> 11:06.286
i-it's horrible!

11:06.320 --> 11:08.454
Other people
live here!

11:08.489 --> 11:10.456
Oh, my God!

11:10.491 --> 11:11.958
How did this happen?!

11:11.992 --> 11:13.293
It's from smoking!

11:13.327 --> 11:14.460
It's not that bad.

11:14.495 --> 11:16.129
Peter, you can't live
like this.

11:16.163 --> 11:17.797
I'm taking you
to Dr. Hartman.

11:17.831 --> 11:19.465
No! I hate the doctor!

11:19.500 --> 11:21.000
Are you sure?

11:21.035 --> 11:22.669
There are Cheez-Its in there.

11:22.703 --> 11:24.571
Cheez-Its?!

11:25.606 --> 11:27.440
Huh? W-Wait. What's going on?

11:27.474 --> 11:29.108
I'm scared! I'm scared!

11:29.143 --> 11:31.177
Oh, it's nighttime.

11:31.211 --> 11:32.912
Good night.

11:36.850 --> 11:39.285
Mr. Griffin, I'm gonna need
to ask you a few questions.

11:39.320 --> 11:41.821
Do you think I can jump
and touch that pipe up there?

11:41.855 --> 11:44.157
I don't know.
The hell I can't!

11:44.191 --> 11:45.491
There, got it.

11:45.526 --> 11:47.493
Yeah, I guess
your fingertips grazed it.

11:47.528 --> 11:49.095
Yeah, that counts
as a dunk.

11:49.129 --> 11:51.764
Dr. Hartman, we're here for you
to help Peter quit smoking.

11:51.799 --> 11:54.100
Mrs. Griffin, I can't do
that. It's an addiction.

11:54.134 --> 11:56.436
I can't even get my
son to quit being gay.

11:56.470 --> 11:58.972
Well, you got to do something!
He's killing himself!

11:59.006 --> 12:01.926
All right, how many Vicodins for
you guys to just leave me alone?

12:01.942 --> 12:03.176
Forty.

12:04.478 --> 12:07.180
Well, it's too bad
Dr. Hartman couldn't help us.

12:07.214 --> 12:09.182
I guess we should go
to the Stop Smoking Clinic

12:09.216 --> 12:11.584
and then maybe get
a couple bottles of wine.

12:16.023 --> 12:18.324
Oh, hey, Stewie.
Ready to go to school?

12:18.359 --> 12:20.660
Well, actually, Chris,
I've got good news.

12:20.694 --> 12:22.662
Aw, I'll take
the bad news first.

12:22.696 --> 12:24.464
No. What? There
is no bad news.

12:24.498 --> 12:26.599
Oh, all right. Then give me
the good news first.

12:26.634 --> 12:29.602
The good news is, I've taught
you everything you need to know

12:29.637 --> 12:30.803
to fend for yourself.

12:30.838 --> 12:33.506
So from now on, you can
go to school without me.

12:33.540 --> 12:34.641
What are you talking about?

12:34.675 --> 12:36.242
I'm running for class president.

12:36.276 --> 12:37.610
I need you!

12:37.645 --> 12:39.112
What are you doing?

12:39.146 --> 12:41.948
You're coming to school with me
whether you like it or not!

12:41.982 --> 12:43.950
Let me out! You can't keep me
in here forever!

12:43.984 --> 12:45.485
I have too many plans
for the future!

12:45.519 --> 12:47.153
I'll never win a Nobel Prize!

12:47.187 --> 12:48.955
I'll never be a member
of Parliament!

12:48.989 --> 12:51.224
I'll never get to express
disappointment with young people

12:51.258 --> 12:53.159
while putting in my dentures!

12:53.193 --> 12:55.028
Stupid younger generation.

12:55.062 --> 12:58.031
Back in my day, we had
Katy Perry, Justin Bieber.

12:58.065 --> 12:59.766
That was real music.

13:10.911 --> 13:12.545
Lois, why do all the people
in here look

13:12.579 --> 13:13.880
like Emperor Palpatine?

13:13.914 --> 13:16.015
Because they're all
heavy smokers, Peter.

13:16.050 --> 13:17.850
I'm gonna sign you in.

13:19.253 --> 13:23.623
Would the driver of a 1978
Camaro please move your car?

13:27.761 --> 13:29.662
Man, how the hell
am I gonna quit smoking?

13:29.697 --> 13:32.699
I wish smoking
could just quit me instead.

13:32.733 --> 13:34.300
Thank you
for meeting me here.

13:34.334 --> 13:36.803
I have something
very important to tell you.

13:36.837 --> 13:38.938
I have something
important to tell you, too.

13:38.972 --> 13:41.941
Peter, I think we
should see other people.

13:42.976 --> 13:44.610
Okay.

13:46.947 --> 13:50.383
Uh, good, that's what
I was gonna say, too.

13:50.417 --> 13:52.985
Excuse me, I'm Mr. Stone
with the ad agency

13:53.020 --> 13:54.987
of Anderson, Wheeler
and Thirdname.

13:55.022 --> 13:58.725
And I think you'd be perfect for
our new anti-smoking campaign.

13:58.759 --> 14:01.260
Me? You'd want me on TV?

14:01.295 --> 14:02.595
Even though I'm hideous?

14:02.629 --> 14:04.530
<i>Sure. Have you seen
Boardwalk Empire?</i>

14:04.565 --> 14:06.933
It's just a crap-fest
of faces.

14:06.967 --> 14:09.535
There is one catch: if you're
gonna be our spokesman,

14:09.570 --> 14:11.204
you have to keep smoking.

14:11.238 --> 14:13.272
We need you to stay wrinkled
and sickly.

14:13.307 --> 14:15.975
But my wife brought me here
to quit smoking.

14:16.009 --> 14:17.710
Wives, huh?

14:17.745 --> 14:19.645
O-Okay,
now I'm on your side!

14:19.680 --> 14:20.847
Oh, this is awesome!

14:20.881 --> 14:22.115
I'm gonna be on TV!

14:22.149 --> 14:24.117
But no more talk
of quitting, right?

14:24.151 --> 14:26.119
You got it. So, um,

14:26.153 --> 14:27.873
does somethin' like this
pay a lot of money?

14:27.888 --> 14:29.856
What do you think
a lot of money is?

14:29.890 --> 14:32.692
I-I don't want to say.
I'm embarrassed.

14:37.117 --> 14:40.086
And now a word from
the American Lung Association.

14:40.120 --> 14:42.455
Oh, hey, hey, guys! Here
comes one of my TV spots!

14:42.489 --> 14:44.724
Hi, Peter Griffin,
sickly smoker.

14:44.758 --> 14:46.793
This is your heart.

14:46.827 --> 14:49.295
This is your heart
on cigarettes.

14:49.330 --> 14:50.797
Any questions?

14:50.864 --> 14:52.599
Yeah, where'd you get
that heart?

14:54.535 --> 14:56.603
Hey, Peter, now that
you're a celebrity,

14:56.637 --> 14:58.605
could I get a picture
of you to put on the wall?

14:58.639 --> 14:59.872
Sure, here you go.

14:59.907 --> 15:01.374
Thanks, man.

15:01.408 --> 15:03.249
I'll put you up next
to these black celebrities

15:03.277 --> 15:05.645
who are just
confusing strangers to you.

15:05.679 --> 15:07.180
Who's Marlin Johnson?

15:07.214 --> 15:09.515
Oh, come on, man.
Stand-up comedian?

15:09.550 --> 15:12.719
He got that whole thing
about the "Oh-Ee-Oh-Ee-Hey-Yo."

15:12.753 --> 15:15.588
I can't even
get through it.

15:15.623 --> 15:17.590
Hey! You talkin'
'bout Marlin Johnson?

15:17.625 --> 15:19.993
You know it!
Oh-Ee-Oh-Ee-Hey-Yo!

15:20.027 --> 15:22.629
That's right.

15:26.500 --> 15:27.800
Hey, Lois.

15:27.835 --> 15:30.403
Peter, I saw your ad on TV,
and I got to say,

15:30.437 --> 15:32.805
I'm glad you're finally
doing the right thing.

15:32.840 --> 15:35.475
Yeah, it feels good
to be helping people.

15:35.509 --> 15:38.144
Peter, what are you doing?!
I thought you quit!

15:38.178 --> 15:40.213
Hey, if George Michael
doesn't have to give up butts,

15:40.247 --> 15:42.248
why should I?

15:44.285 --> 15:47.186
I'm serious.
You have to stop smoking!

15:47.221 --> 15:49.141
Have you looked in the mirror?
You look terrible.

15:49.156 --> 15:50.590
Eh, what do you care?

15:50.624 --> 15:52.992
It's not like you have to look
at my face when we have sex.

15:53.027 --> 15:55.194
Not since we started
role-playing.

15:55.229 --> 15:57.196
Peter, I'm ready.

15:57.231 --> 15:59.999
Okay, now put on yours.

16:00.034 --> 16:03.336
Wow, isn't it weird that
we both picked Mario Lopez?

16:03.370 --> 16:05.605
Yes, Peter.
It's very weird.

16:05.639 --> 16:09.509
Yeah, it shows that we both
go Latino but soft Latino.

16:13.080 --> 16:16.316
Day five of my imprisonment
inside Chris' backpack.

16:16.350 --> 16:18.484
Feces and the buildup thereof
continues to be

16:18.519 --> 16:19.886
my number one problem.

16:19.920 --> 16:22.288
I think a teacher saw me
the other day but said nothing.

16:22.323 --> 16:24.090
I waved and he looked away.

16:30.531 --> 16:33.166
This could be my chance
to escape this canvas cage!

16:44.411 --> 16:46.546
That sounds like an open door.
Which way is out?

16:46.580 --> 16:48.414
God, I love walking
in the hall!

16:48.449 --> 16:49.782
There! That way!

16:52.419 --> 16:53.720
Must escape!

16:55.989 --> 16:58.324
Must... escape.

17:01.595 --> 17:04.330
Mu...

17:05.332 --> 17:08.234
You're gonna die in there.

17:11.271 --> 17:13.106
Welcome back,
Mr. Griffin!

17:13.140 --> 17:14.374
You look terrible!

17:14.408 --> 17:15.975
Thanks, man named Sandy!

17:16.009 --> 17:17.977
Oh, hey, uh, you know,
I don't know if you're the guy

17:18.011 --> 17:19.979
to talk to about this,
but when I went to my trailer

17:20.013 --> 17:22.515
this morning, there was
a hairy naked guy in it.

17:22.549 --> 17:23.850
We don't provide trailers.

17:23.884 --> 17:25.510
We're just next door
to a trailer park.

17:25.535 --> 17:26.085
Ah.

17:26.086 --> 17:28.855
That would explain the violent
lovemaking that followed.

17:28.889 --> 17:30.456
Listen, Peter, we need to talk.

17:30.491 --> 17:33.926
I'm sorry to tell you this, but
we no longer need your services.

17:33.961 --> 17:35.395
Wait... What?

17:35.429 --> 17:37.330
How could you do that?!

17:37.364 --> 17:38.731
Well, I went to a NASCAR event

17:38.766 --> 17:41.200
and realized you're just
an average-looking man.

17:41.235 --> 17:42.869
Please! I'll do anything
to keep my job!

17:42.903 --> 17:44.704
N-Name anything you want
and I'll do it!

17:44.738 --> 17:46.739
Touch your toes.

17:49.176 --> 17:51.144
Please give me
something else!

17:51.178 --> 17:54.147
I'm sorry, Peter,
it's over.

17:57.084 --> 17:59.719
Why are your eyes
crying, Peter?

17:59.753 --> 18:01.320
They fired me, Larry!

18:01.355 --> 18:04.323
Come on. Let's go kidnap
my neighbor's dog

18:04.358 --> 18:07.226
and tell them
we don't have it.

18:12.766 --> 18:14.467
Good morning, students.

18:14.501 --> 18:17.136
First of all, I don't care
what the courts say,

18:17.171 --> 18:19.138
let's thank
the Christian god together.

18:19.173 --> 18:20.940
Now then, we're here today

18:20.974 --> 18:23.142
for the presidential candidate
debate.

18:23.177 --> 18:25.678
Okay, remember,
people think I'm smart now.

18:25.712 --> 18:28.014
So it's got to be clever
and it's got to pop.

18:28.048 --> 18:30.283
I'm done! I'm not
saying another word.

18:30.317 --> 18:32.218
You can't hold me prisoner
in here forever!

18:32.252 --> 18:35.621
Why not?
Name one person who loves you.

18:35.656 --> 18:39.592
Wow. Not a
proportional response.

18:39.626 --> 18:41.794
All right, let's begin
with an opening statement

18:41.829 --> 18:45.264
from the perpetually upbeat
black kid.

18:45.299 --> 18:46.539
Thanks for letting me go first.

18:46.567 --> 18:48.768
I got an hour-and-a-half drive
home after this.

18:48.802 --> 18:50.436
You're not getting it,
Chris, are you?

18:50.471 --> 18:52.505
You were being bullied
day in and day out,

18:52.539 --> 18:53.940
so I tried to help you.

18:53.974 --> 18:55.541
I tried to be a good brother.

18:55.576 --> 18:57.343
And you've repaid me with abuse.

18:57.377 --> 18:59.846
You're the bully, Chris Griffin.

19:02.883 --> 19:05.418
Oh, my God.
You're right.

19:07.754 --> 19:11.724
And now an opening
statement from our second candidate,

19:11.758 --> 19:14.260
the King of the Zingers,
Chris Griffin.

19:16.797 --> 19:18.431
Go easy on me, Chris.

19:18.465 --> 19:20.433
My sister has M.S.

19:20.467 --> 19:22.702
I'm worried what you're
gonna do with that.

19:22.736 --> 19:25.037
I'm out. I'm not running.

19:25.072 --> 19:26.639
And neither is she.

19:26.673 --> 19:28.474
I knew you'd
have something.

19:28.509 --> 19:29.809
No, you don't understand.

19:29.843 --> 19:31.978
I'm dropping out
of the election.

19:33.313 --> 19:34.614
I'm a big fraud,

19:34.648 --> 19:36.616
and I've treated people
terribly.

19:36.650 --> 19:40.419
Much like Jeff Zucker
when he ran NBC.

19:41.455 --> 19:42.588
I'm sorry, Stewie.

19:42.623 --> 19:43.923
Can you forgive me?

19:43.957 --> 19:46.759
Well, I may no longer be
on your back,

19:46.793 --> 19:50.096
but I'll always be on your side.

19:53.000 --> 19:54.967
All right,

19:55.002 --> 19:57.169
this election is postponed.
Go back to class.

19:57.204 --> 19:58.504
Oh, and another thing,

19:58.539 --> 20:00.973
stop making fun of teachers
who don't have cars.

20:01.008 --> 20:05.144
Life's not as easy as you think
it's gonna be right now.

20:10.817 --> 20:13.786
You know, Chris, what you did on
that stage took a lot of guts.

20:13.820 --> 20:15.187
Thanks, Stewie.

20:15.222 --> 20:17.723
And thanks to you, I'm no
longer getting bullied.

20:17.758 --> 20:18.925
Well, that's great.

20:18.959 --> 20:21.127
I guess we put those bullies
in their place, huh?

20:21.161 --> 20:23.329
Yeah. Two of them
shot themselves.

20:23.363 --> 20:25.698
Oh, that's so good
to hear, Chris.

20:25.732 --> 20:27.867
Are they done?
They're-they're all done?

20:27.901 --> 20:29.402
Okay, all right,
let's finish ours.

20:29.436 --> 20:33.005
Well, I finally quit smoking and
I'm ready to go back to normal!

20:33.040 --> 20:34.607
Peter, that's not
how it works.

20:34.641 --> 20:36.943
The damage you've done
is irreversible.

20:36.977 --> 20:39.278
Yeah, Lois is right.
As bad as you look,

20:39.313 --> 20:41.881
the damage you've done
to your heart and your lungs is,

20:41.915 --> 20:44.216
no doubt, exponentially worse.
What?!

20:44.251 --> 20:47.431
Well, try cuttin' to the outside
of the house over some music.

20:47.432 --> 20:49.400
That usually works.

20:49.401 --> 21:50.401
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru